      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am answering my own question.\n\nI verified that `seq_params-\u003eseq_level_idx[i]` is only used here to set `seq_params-\u003eop_params[i].bitrate`.\n\n`seq_params-\u003eop_params[i].bitrate` is only used at line 187 to set `seq_params-\u003eop_params[i].buffer_size`.\n\nThen, `seq_params-\u003eop_params[i].bitrate` and `seq_params-\u003eop_params[i].buffer_size` are not used again.\n\nI also verified that `av1_max_level_bitrate()` returns the same result (`UNDEFINED_RATE` \u003d 1 \u003c\u003c 21) for an undefined level and for the maximum parameters level (31).\n\nSo we conclude that after this CL, libaom treats an undefined level and the maximum parameters level (31) in the same way, except in the if-else statement at lines 159-162.",
